            <ArticleTitle>Forgotten needle--an unusual cause of chronic pelvic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">A case presented with chronic pelvic pain since a Fothergills repair 9 years back. Over the years she had received multiple courses of antibiotics and anti-inflammatory drugs to no avail.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Thorough evaluation revealed the presence of a foreign body in the form of a surgical needle in the cervix.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
